Package: beats
Version: 1.4.0
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, librsvg2-common, hicolor-icon-theme, desktop-file-utils, pipewire, pipewire-pulse, pipewire-bin, wireplumber, libpipewire-0.3-modules, libspa-0.2-modules, libspa-0.2-bluetooth, pulseaudio-utils, alsa-utils, pkexec | policykit-1, ca-certificates
Recommends: bluez
Replaces: headset-mic-fixer
Conflicts: headset-mic-fixer
Provides: headset-mic-fixer
Maintainer: You <you@example.com>
Description: Fix noisy headset and earbud microphones on PipeWire
 Beats is a dark GTK tool to pick the right mic/port, see a live level
 meter, tune gain and hardware Mic Boost, add a noise filter (light,
 WebRTC "Strong", or RNNoise "Maximum"), fix Bluetooth headset profile
 problems (mSBC, auto-switching) and stop audio power-save clicks.
 Installed system-wide with a menu launcher. Maximum mode is bundled.
